<p>President Donald Trump met German Chancellor Friedrich Merz at the White House as the U.S.-Israel conflict with Iran widened, putting allied coordination—and frictions—on clear display. Trump publicly thanked Merz, saying Germany had been “helping out” by giving U.S. forces access to certain bases, and the two leaders discussed Iran, trade, and Russia’s war in Ukraine. In the Oval Office, Trump also used the meeting to take swipes at other European partners—threatening to “embargo” Spain over defense spending and its condemnation of U.S. strikes on Iran, and taking aim at UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer. Politico described Merz as mostly silent in public, part of a strategy to avoid contradicting Trump on camera while trying to influence him in private—an approach that could carry political costs at home and across Europe. Merz, for his part, struck a more forward-looking note, saying Germany is “looking forward to the day after” the Iran war ends. Even with the tense rhetoric, the talks showed Washington and Berlin still have working channels—an important, if imperfect, base for negotiating next steps on security, tariffs, and Ukraine.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TTlm12O24jZg5YZK9BE8SFHkBKKmgqKylYmDfkZiPBE-xrdDJIqC_Ic01PgI9mtVSME4xIBXH9AmhrzXQniXpjfxiSolFeZQmiJ4KLGrNxijWK-27Y-F_eKwOvZ8FSPurXl9SJg20nUQDlGWI2qAKEdKeP0EUT3CuPzaWxKXDkL24tbPuxnFNNjGfLaMMz897ovQGKg7kXvZU3b9JP_0I12Ni3_HL50v-2X_mBOChxrQAKdJroJ0PPKIz0HOmOWtsur0zvUGQ5NQOFrvmg' alt='US President Donald Trump meets with German Chancellor Friedrich Merz in the Oval Office of the White House in Washington on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Thank-you and comparisons: Trump thanked Merz and said Germany had been “helping out” by granting U.S. forces access to certain bases, while also contrasting Germany’s approach with Britain’s and Spain’s.</li><li>Tariffs on camera: Trump again suggested he could escalate the trade fight with Europe. Coverage noted he sometimes waffled or left details unclear while discussing tariffs in the same appearance.</li><li>China mention: In the same appearance, Trump praised China while discussing tariffs and defending the Iran strikes.</li><li>Optics and political risk: Politico said Merz’s visible deference—staying mostly silent as Trump berated other European leaders—looked “humiliating” and could carry political costs, even if it creates space for private persuasion.</li></ul><blockquote>Looking forward to the day after - Friedrich Merz</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Friedrich Merz (Germany): Merz emphasized planning for what comes after the Iran conflict, pointing to postwar stabilization and reconstruction once the fighting ends. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-trump-meets-with-germanys-merz-as-u-s-israel-conflict-with-iran-widens'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump (United States): Trump said he was justified in ordering attacks on Iran and argued they prevented a “nuclear war,” while also criticizing European allies and talking about tariffs. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/diplomacy/article/3345327/trump-says-hell-cut-trade-spain-over-iran-war-stance'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Politico Europe analysis: Politico focused on the visuals, describing Merz as “powerless” and “obsequious” on camera as Trump lashed out at Spain and the UK, and argued the display could unsettle voters in Germany and other European capitals. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/friedrich-merz-powerless-oval-office-donald-trump-attacks-europe-allies/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>Deutsche Welle reporting: DW said Iran dominated the agenda in Merz’s second meeting with Trump, with tariffs and Ukraine also on the table. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-and-merz-discuss-iran-tariffs-and-ukraine/live-76199914'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/friedrich-merz-powerless-oval-office-donald-trump-attacks-europe-allies/'>Germany’s Merz sits powerless as Trump attacks European allies in Oval Office</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-live-trump-meets-with-germanys-merz-as-u-s-israel-conflict-with-iran-widens'>WATCH: Trump meets with Germany&#x27;s Merz as U.S.-Israel conflict with Iran widens</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-germany-helping-with-iran-strikes-meets-merz-at-white-house/article70700965.ece'>Trump says Germany helping with Iran strikes, meets Merz at White House</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-trump-hosts-germanys-merz-against-backdrop-of-iran-war-and-tariff/'>Trump hosts Germany’s Merz against backdrop of Iran war and tariff threats</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-and-merz-discuss-iran-tariffs-and-ukraine/live-76199914'>Trump and Merz discuss Iran, tariffs and Ukraine</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-says-germany-helping-with-iran-strikes-thanks-merz-at-white-house'>Trump says Germany helping with Iran strikes, thanks Merz at White House</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/diplomacy/article/3345327/trump-says-hell-cut-trade-spain-over-iran-war-stance'>Trump slams European allies, praises China and continues to justify Iran attack</a> - scmp.com</li></ul>